.TH GIT-TIDY 1 "2026-07-29" "git-tidy" "Git Extensions"
.SH NAME
git-tidy \- keep a directory full of git checkouts clean
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git tidy
[\fB\-C\fR \fIDIR\fR] [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-i\fR|\fB\-\-apply\fR] [\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR]
\fIsync\fR|\fIprune\fR|\fIclean\fR|\fItrash\fR|\fIdoctor\fR|\fIrun\fR|\fIinit\fR|\fIconfig\fR|\fIrestore\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
Fetches every repository under a directory, puts each back on the branch its
remote calls default, deletes the local branches whose upstream is gone, and
reclaims the space build tools left behind.
.PP
Nothing is modified without \fB\-\-ask\fR or \fB\-\-apply\fR.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B sync
Fetch, prune remote-tracking refs, switch to the default branch, fast-forward.
Never merges, never rebases. A repository that has diverged is reported.
.TP
.B prune
Delete local branches whose upstream is gone from the remote, but only once
their commits are contained in the default branch. Unpushed work is reported.
.TP
.B clean
Remove build output and caches. With \fBclean.ignored\fR, everything
.B .gitignore
already calls disposable. A tracked file is never deleted, unless
\fIclean.tracked\fR says so.
.TP
.B trash
Sweep loose junk in the workspace into a timestamped quarantine with a
manifest. Off until a config turns it on.
.TP
.B doctor
Report what needs a human: credentials in remote URLs, detached HEADs,
unpushed commits, repositories with no remote. Changes nothing, unless
.B \-\-fix
says otherwise.
.TP
.B \-\-fix
On
.B doctor
or
.BR run :
also carry out the remedies that cannot cost a commit \(em put a detached HEAD
back on the trunk, take the credential out of a remote URL, pack an oversized
.IR .git .
Still a dry run until \fB\-\-apply\fR.
.IP
A detached HEAD is only moved when its commit is already contained in the trunk;
otherwise that HEAD is the work, and switching away would leave it reachable
from the reflog alone. Not moved either with uncommitted changes, or when the
trunk is checked out in another worktree. Unpushed commits and local-only
branches are never touched: only you know whether they should be pushed or
dropped.
.TP
.B run
sync, prune, clean, trash and doctor, in that order. A
.BR clean ,
.B trash
or
.B run
that applies anything also drops quarantines older than
\fItrash.retention_days\fR; 0 keeps them for ever.
.IP
If three remotes in a row cannot be reached \(em remotes, not checkouts, and one
fetch that works starts the count again \(em the run stops rather than working
through the rest on the same timeout, and points at the VPN, the proxy, DNS and
the SSH agent. This applies to
.B sync
as well. A repository that is gone, or one you may not read, is not the network
and does not count.
.B clean
and
.B trash
do not need the network.
.TP
.B init
Write a commented configuration file:
.B \-\-global
for
.IR ~/.config/git\-tidy/config.yaml ,
.B \-\-path
.I DIR
for a
.I .git\-tidy.yaml
in one directory. Asks a short set of questions when there is somebody to ask;
.B \-q
writes the plain template instead, and
.B \-n
prints it without writing.
.TP
.B config
Print the effective configuration for any path.
.TP
.B restore
Put quarantined files back. Takes a timestamp to restore just one sweep,
.B \-\-list
to see what is held and stop, and
.B \-\-expire
to delete the quarantines older than \fItrash.retention_days\fR \(em the only
part of restore that removes anything. Nothing is ever restored over a file
that is already there.
.SH MODES
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
The default. Print what would happen and change nothing.
.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-ask
Confirm every change: y, n, a (all of this kind), s (skip this kind),
Y (everything), q (stop). Runs single-threaded so the prompts do not interleave.
.TP
.B \-\-apply
Carry every change out without asking.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-force
The only flag here that can lose work, and it does exactly two things: it
deletes a branch whose upstream is gone even when its commits are not in the
trunk (still only after a fetch succeeded in the same run), and it stashes
uncommitted changes so a repository can be switched and fast-forwarded. Nothing
is discarded \(em the report says which stash holds the work.
.IP
It deliberately cannot delete a directory containing a git repository \(em
except the caches named in \fIclean.regenerable\fR, whose nested repositories
are a tool's own clones \(em cannot hard-delete anything matching
.I trash.sensitive
or
.IR clean.ignored_keep ,
and cannot remove a tracked file, follow a symlink or reach outside the
workspace. Pair it with \-\-ask the first time.
.IP
.I clean.ignored_keep
has one carve-out, which
.I trash.sensitive
does not: inside a path named in
.IR clean.regenerable ,
it does not apply. Those are caches a tool rebuilds, and every
.I .terraform
holds a
.I terraform.tfstate
that is the backend pointer rather than your state.
.IP
A file with a source-code extension is exempt from
.I trash.sensitive
alone: a
.I tokenizer.js
matches
.I *token*
and is not a secret. The exemption does not apply to
.IR clean.ignored_keep ,
whose entries name local files that are deliberately not in git \(em a
.I secrets.py
is exactly what that list is for.
.TP
.BR \-C ", " \-\-workspace " " \fIDIR\fR
The directory holding the repositories. Defaults to the current one.
.TP
.BR \-j ", " \-\-jobs " " \fIN\fR
How much to do at once. The default is one worker per CPU core.
.TP
.BR \-\-include ", " \-\-exclude " " \fIGLOB\fR
Limit which repositories are touched. Repeatable.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the report as JSON.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print every path, rather than one line per repository. This is what the
"\-v shows each one" in the summary refers to.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Print the summary and nothing else.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Never colour the output. Colour is off anyway when stdout is not a terminal,
or when
.I NO_COLOR
is set.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/git-tidy/config.yaml
Global configuration.
.TP
.I .git\-tidy.yaml
Per-directory configuration, in the workspace root or any directory down to a
single repository. Merged over the global file; the deepest one wins.
.TP
.I .git\-tidy\-trash/
Quarantine, one timestamped directory per sweep, each with a manifest.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if anything failed, 2 on a usage or configuration error.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git\-clean (1),
.BR git\-fetch (1),
.BR git\-worktree (1)
.PP
https://github.com/sapn95/git-tidy
